    {"path": "src/maxim/embodied_runtime/selfy.py", "reason": "The `Maxim` robot-runtime class: its constructor sets the process-wide multiprocessing start method, probes the GPU, builds a segmentation model and connects to a robot through the hardware registry, and it composes the six embodied_runtime mixins that are measured on their own. Omitted since 2b77c3d6 (2026-02-07, 'too coupled for unit testing'); four unit tests reach parts of it (operational-mode launch, workspace safety, robots.yaml connect config, swallowed-log) but its lines are not counted. Not covered by the model-cache nightly.", "covered_by": null, "ref": null},
    {"path": "src/maxim/simulation/tty_stdin.py", "reason": "ONLY the simulation's termios/TTY raw-mode read loops (stdin_reader_raw, the sim.stdin thread's interactive-mode target, and read_post_sim_goal_raw, the post-sim new-goal prompt) plus the state that exists only for them (the escape-sequence keymap and the terminal-restore record with its atexit/SIGTERM hook). Every line needs a real TTY on stdin, so the fast suite cannot reach it (the orchestrator characterization arms never enter the raw loops: the new_goal arm runs interactive ON on a stdin that passes stdin_reader_raw's isatty check but whose fileno() raises, so the head of stdin_reader_raw runs and falls back to the line reader before raw mode, and it fakes read_post_sim_goal_raw; every other arm runs non-interactive). Moved verbatim out of orchestrator.py::start_simulation_mode in slice 0 of the 1.3.2 orchestrator decomposition (owner decisions (e) and SF-4, 2026-10-13), apart from the closure-to-keyword-parameter rewrite. Nothing else may live in this file. Not strictly unreachable: a POSIX test could drive it through pty.openpty(); dropping this exclusion later is a ledger-legal shrink.", "covered_by": null, "ref": "#947"}
